        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3c3ec047-d108-5cde-84bf-f28755272e55",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: The Justice Collective\n- Events: Hillsborough disaster\n- Places: Hillsborough football stadium, Sheffield, England, Leppings Lane stand\n- Topics: fund-raising records, associated charities, FA Cup semi-final\n\nFacts:\n- On 15 April 1989, the Hillsborough disaster was a human crush at Hillsborough football stadium in Sheffield, England, during the 1988–89 FA Cup semi-final between Liverpool and Nottingham Forest.\n- The Hillsborough disaster occurred in the two standing-only central pens in the Leppings Lane stand that were allocated to Liverpool supporters.\n- In 2012, The Justice Collective was originally established as a fund-raising record to raise money for charities associated with the Hillsborough disaster.\n- The Justice Collective is a collective of musicians and celebrities.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
